{#-
  PASS 3 — user prompt, one render per paper.

  The paper is described by its pass-1 labels rather than by its text, which is
  what makes this pass cheap enough to re-run every time you edit the taxonomy.

  Available here:
    taxonomy   the areas, rendered with their definitions and subtopics
    areas      just the names
    paper      one pass-1 record; paper._display[field] is the same value
               formatted for a prompt (lists joined, missing values as "n/a")
    extra_fields, project
-#}
TAXONOMY

{{ taxonomy }}

PAPER

Title: {{ paper._display.title }}
One-line summary: {{ paper._display.one_line_summary }}
Topic labels from a first reading: {{ paper._display.main_topic }}; {{ paper._display.subtopics }}
Task: {{ paper._display.task }}
Method: {{ paper._display.method_family }}
Contribution type: {{ paper._display.contribution_type }}
{% for field in extra_fields %}
{{ field.name }}: {{ paper._display[field.name] }}
{% endfor %}

Assign this paper:

- main_area: exactly one area name from the taxonomy.
- secondary_area: a second area name, or "none" if the paper sits squarely in one.
- subtopics: 2-4 subtopic labels. Prefer subtopics listed under the chosen area
  in the taxonomy; only add a new one if nothing listed fits.
- confidence: 0.0-1.0 that main_area is right.
- why: one short sentence.
